Chapter: Reservoir
  cites Foreword chapter Random

 Reservoir sampling (Vitter's Algorithm R). Maintains a fixed-size
 random sample from a stream of unknown length. Each item has equal
 probability of being in the sample. O(1) per item, O(k) space.

 We say:

Section: Types
  ReservoirSample = record {
    rs-items : List Integer,
    rs-capacity : Integer between 1 and 65535,
    rs-count : Integer between 0 and 65535,
    rs-seen : Integer
  }

Section: Construction
  reservoir-new : Integer -> ReservoirSample
  reservoir-new (k) = ReservoirSample { rs-items = [], rs-capacity = __narrow k, rs-count = 0, rs-seen = 0 }

Section: Sampling
  reservoir-add : ReservoirSample, Integer, Integer -> ReservoirSample
  reservoir-add (rs) (item) (seed) =
    let n = rs.rs-seen + 1
    in if rs.rs-count < rs.rs-capacity then
      ReservoirSample { rs-items = list-push (rs.rs-items) item, rs-capacity = rs.rs-capacity, rs-count = rs.rs-count + 1, rs-seen = n }
    else let j = reservoir-rand seed n
    in if j < rs.rs-capacity then
      ReservoirSample { rs-items = list-set-at (rs.rs-items) j item, rs-capacity = rs.rs-capacity, rs-count = rs.rs-count, rs-seen = n }
    else ReservoirSample { rs-items = rs.rs-items, rs-capacity = rs.rs-capacity, rs-count = rs.rs-count, rs-seen = n }

  reservoir-add-all : ReservoirSample, List Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> ReservoirSample
  reservoir-add-all (rs) (items) (seed) (i) (len) =
    if i >= len then rs
    else reservoir-add-all (reservoir-add rs (list-at items i) (seed + i * 7919)) items seed (i + 1) len

Section: Helpers
 The whole promise of Algorithm R is that every item that goes past has the
 SAME probability of being in the sample. That rests entirely on this draw
 being uniform over [0, n).

 reservoir-rand used to be `bit-xor (seed * 2654435761) (n * 40503)` and then
 the remainder, with no downward fold. Multiplication carries entropy upward
 only, so the keep-or-drop decision at position n was a function of the low
 bits of the seed and of n. A sampler whose acceptance is a parity stripe is
 not sampling.

 Measured before the change by `codex/test/reservoir-uniform.codex`: twenty
 items through a five-slot reservoir over 200 seeds, expecting each item to
 survive about 50 times. Item 7 survived 12 times and item 1 survived 78.

  reservoir-rand : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  reservoir-rand (seed) (n) = rand-in-range seed n 0 (n - 1)

Section: Queries
  reservoir-items : ReservoirSample -> List Integer
  reservoir-items (rs) = rs.rs-items

  reservoir-count : ReservoirSample -> Integer
  reservoir-count (rs) = rs.rs-count

  reservoir-seen : ReservoirSample -> Integer
  reservoir-seen (rs) = rs.rs-seen

